VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in the canvas, you\'ll open up a little node search box, and you\'ll see all the different types of nodes. So, you\'ll have inputs, all the basic stuff, text, images, and numbers. I appreciate that they\'re actually sorted like this'

[20:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'because they don\'t make a difference whether it\'s, you know, a type of media asset like a video or audio, or even just something like number or text. It\'s different in other UIs, so very, very good idea to sort them like that. And'

[20:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this is where it starts getting really interesting. So, they actually put workflows into nodes rather than technical functionality. So, let\'s say if in ComfyUI, you have a node that like just loads an AI model, that sort of'

[21:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'feature will be inside another node here in Atlas because we don\'t think in technical features like that. We think in how do we get from A to B. So here you\'ll have text to image fast as a node in itself. So that\'s just one node with'

[21:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the prompt in there, the resolution, the engine, so the actual model, and in the end you\'ll have an image. So that\'s all in one node. Really, really cool. Of course, if you want to input the prompt'

